{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"embedded-languages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embedded Languages"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An embedded language is a range owned by one language but tokenized by another registered definition."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Markup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML, Vue, and Svelte recognize script and style regions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script>\n  const ready = true\n</script>\n\n<style>\n  .button { color: red }\n</style>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register each tokenizer you want used:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, ts, vue],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" bodies use JavaScript. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">"},{"type":"text","value":" uses TypeScript. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<style>"},{"type":"text","value":" uses CSS."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the target definition is absent, the body remains plain text while the outer markup still highlights."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"compare-embedded-languages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compare embedded languages"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Switch the outer language to see registered JavaScript, TypeScript, and CSS tokenizers handle each embedded region."}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"highlight-embedded-languages-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"highlight-embedded-languages","data-collapsed-indexes":"[]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/main.ts\",\"environment\":\"client\",\"files\":{\"/src/main.ts\":\"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\\nimport { markdown } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/markdown'\\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\\n\\nconst samples = {\\n  html: [\\n    '<script>',\\n    '  const ready = true',\\n    '</script>',\\n    '',\\n    '<style>',\\n    '  .button { color: tomato }',\\n    '</style>',\\n  ].join('\\\\n'),\\n  vue: [\\n    '<script lang=\\\"ts\\\">',\\n    '  const user: { name: string } = { name: \\\"Ada\\\" }',\\n    '</script>',\\n    '',\\n    '<template><p>{{ user.name }}</p></template>',\\n  ].join('\\\\n'),\\n  markdown: [\\n    '# Typed button',\\n    '',\\n    '```tsx',\\n    'const button = <button>Save</button>',\\n    '```',\\n  ].join('\\\\n'),\\n}\\n\\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\\n  languages: [css, html, js, markdown, ts, tsx, vue],\\n})\\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\\n  light: githubLightTheme,\\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\\n})\\n\\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\\n.demo { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\\n.tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); }\\n.tabs button { padding: 6px 10px; border: 0; border-radius: 7px; background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }\\n.tabs button[aria-pressed=\\\"true\\\"] { background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 12%, transparent); font-weight: 600; }\\npre.th-code { margin: 0; min-height: 180px; }\\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }`\\n\\n  document.head.append(style)\\n  output.innerHTML = `<section class=\\\"demo\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"tabs\\\">\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" data-lang=\\\"html\\\" aria-pressed=\\\"true\\\">HTML</button>\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" data-lang=\\\"vue\\\" aria-pressed=\\\"false\\\">Vue</button>\\n    <button type=\\\"button\\\" data-lang=\\\"markdown\\\" aria-pressed=\\\"false\\\">Markdown</button>\\n  </div>\\n  <div class=\\\"output\\\"></div>\\n</section>`\\n\\n  const codeOutput = output.querySelector('.output')\\n  const buttons = output.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang]')\\n\\n  function renderLanguage(lang: keyof typeof samples) {\\n    if (!(codeOutput instanceof HTMLElement)) return\\n    codeOutput.innerHTML = highlighter.highlight(samples[lang], { lang }).html\\n    buttons.forEach((button) => {\\n      button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.lang === lang))\\n    })\\n  }\\n\\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\\n    button.addEventListener('click', () => {\\n      const lang = button.dataset.lang\\n      if (lang === 'html' || lang === 'vue' || lang === 'markdown') {\\n        renderLanguage(lang)\\n      }\\n    })\\n  })\\n\\n  renderLanguage('html')\\n}\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { markdown } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/markdown'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\n\nconst samples = {\n  html: [\n    '<script>',\n    '  const ready = true',\n    '</script>',\n    '',\n    '<style>',\n    '  .button { color: tomato }',\n    '</style>',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n  vue: [\n    '<script lang=\"ts\">',\n    '  const user: { name: string } = { name: \"Ada\" }',\n    '</script>',\n    '',\n    '<template><p>{{ user.name }}</p></template>',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n  markdown: [\n    '# Typed button',\n    '',\n    '```tsx',\n    'const button = <button>Save</button>',\n    '```',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n}\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, markdown, ts, tsx, vue],\n})\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\n  light: githubLightTheme,\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\n})\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\n.demo { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\n.tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); }\n.tabs button { padding: 6px 10px; border: 0; border-radius: 7px; background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }\n.tabs button[aria-pressed=\"true\"] { background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 12%, transparent); font-weight: 600; }\npre.th-code { margin: 0; min-height: 180px; }\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }`\n\n  document.head.append(style)\n  output.innerHTML = `<section class=\"demo\">\n  <div class=\"tabs\">\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"html\" aria-pressed=\"true\">HTML</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"vue\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Vue</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"markdown\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Markdown</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"output\"></div>\n</section>`\n\n  const codeOutput = output.querySelector('.output')\n  const buttons = output.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang]')\n\n  function renderLanguage(lang: keyof typeof samples) {\n    if (!(codeOutput instanceof HTMLElement)) return\n    codeOutput.innerHTML = highlighter.highlight(samples[lang], { lang }).html\n    buttons.forEach((button) => {\n      button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.lang === lang))\n    })\n  }\n\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\n    button.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      const lang = button.dataset.lang\n      if (lang === 'html' || lang === 'vue' || lang === 'markdown') {\n        renderLanguage(lang)\n      }\n    })\n  })\n\n  renderLanguage('html')\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"group=highlight-embedded-languages file=/src/main.ts entry env=client","title":"/src/main.ts","file":"/src/main.ts"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"vue-expressions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue expressions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue moustache expressions delegate to JavaScript when it is registered:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<p>{{ user.name }}</p>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"svelte-expressions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte expressions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte brace expressions delegate to JavaScript. Svelte control tags remain markup control syntax rather than ordinary JavaScript expressions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ejs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"EJS"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"EJS regions delegate to JavaScript when available:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<% if (user) { %>\n  <h1><%= user.name %></h1>\n<% } %>","lang":"ejs"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"php","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PHP"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"php"},{"type":"text","value":" to highlight PHP code, including tagless excerpts. Inputs containing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<?php"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<?="},{"type":"text","value":" are treated as documents, with text outside the PHP tags delegated to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"html"},{"type":"text","value":" only when it is registered. Legacy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<?"},{"type":"text","value":" short tags aren't recognized."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { php } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/php'\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [php, html] })\nconst result = highlighter.highlight('<p><?= $name ?></p>', { lang: 'php' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PHP does not import HTML. Register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"js"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"css"},{"type":"text","value":" too when the surrounding HTML contains script or style blocks. Quoted strings, including interpolation, and heredoc/nowdoc bodies stay string tokens; Highlight doesn't parse the expressions inside them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"markdown-fences","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Markdown fences"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Markdown definition reads the fence info string and delegates the body:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"```tsx\nconst node = <Button />\n```","lang":"md"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markdown"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" must be registered. Unknown fence languages receive the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code-inline"},{"type":"text","value":" class without another tokenizer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"recursive-template-interpolation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recursive template interpolation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JavaScript and TypeScript templates are recursive rather than cross-language embeddings:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const label = `Hello ${user.name.toUpperCase()} ${`#${count}`}`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"String chunks remain strings. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"${"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"}"},{"type":"text","value":" are operators, and expression bodies return to the script tokenizer, including nested templates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-dependencies-are-optional","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why dependencies are optional"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Making HTML import JavaScript and CSS would be convenient but would defeat selective modules. Optional delegation keeps import cost explicit and lets a site register one shared JavaScript definition for HTML, Vue, Svelte, EJS, and Markdown."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a focused delegation system, not a general recursive grammar DSL. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../architecture","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Architecture"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the boundary."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"embedded-languages","text":"Embedded Languages","level":1},{"id":"markup","text":"Markup","level":2},{"id":"compare-embedded-languages","text":"Compare embedded languages","level":2},{"id":"vue-expressions","text":"Vue expressions","level":2},{"id":"svelte-expressions","text":"Svelte expressions","level":2},{"id":"ejs","text":"EJS","level":2},{"id":"php","text":"PHP","level":2},{"id":"markdown-fences","text":"Markdown fences","level":2},{"id":"recursive-template-interpolation","text":"Recursive template interpolation","level":2},{"id":"why-dependencies-are-optional","text":"Why dependencies are optional","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Embedded Languages\n\nAn embedded language is a range owned by one language but tokenized by another registered definition.\n\n## Markup\n\nHTML, Vue, and Svelte recognize script and style regions:\n\n```html\n<script>\n  const ready = true\n</script>\n\n<style>\n  .button { color: red }\n</style>\n```\n\nRegister each tokenizer you want used:\n\n```ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, ts, vue],\n})\n```\n\nDefault `<script>` bodies use JavaScript. `<script lang=\"ts\">` uses TypeScript. `<style>` uses CSS.\n\nIf the target definition is absent, the body remains plain text while the outer markup still highlights.\n\n## Compare embedded languages\n\nSwitch the outer language to see registered JavaScript, TypeScript, and CSS tokenizers handle each embedded region.\n\n```ts group=highlight-embedded-languages file=/src/main.ts entry env=client\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { markdown } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/markdown'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\n\nconst samples = {\n  html: [\n    '<script>',\n    '  const ready = true',\n    '</script>',\n    '',\n    '<style>',\n    '  .button { color: tomato }',\n    '</style>',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n  vue: [\n    '<script lang=\"ts\">',\n    '  const user: { name: string } = { name: \"Ada\" }',\n    '</script>',\n    '',\n    '<template><p>{{ user.name }}</p></template>',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n  markdown: [\n    '# Typed button',\n    '',\n    '```tsx',\n    'const button = <button>Save</button>',\n    '```',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n}\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, markdown, ts, tsx, vue],\n})\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\n  light: githubLightTheme,\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\n})\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\n.demo { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\n.tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); }\n.tabs button { padding: 6px 10px; border: 0; border-radius: 7px; background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }\n.tabs button[aria-pressed=\"true\"] { background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 12%, transparent); font-weight: 600; }\npre.th-code { margin: 0; min-height: 180px; }\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }`\n\n  document.head.append(style)\n  output.innerHTML = `<section class=\"demo\">\n  <div class=\"tabs\">\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"html\" aria-pressed=\"true\">HTML</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"vue\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Vue</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"markdown\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Markdown</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"output\"></div>\n</section>`\n\n  const codeOutput = output.querySelector('.output')\n  const buttons = output.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang]')\n\n  function renderLanguage(lang: keyof typeof samples) {\n    if (!(codeOutput instanceof HTMLElement)) return\n    codeOutput.innerHTML = highlighter.highlight(samples[lang], { lang }).html\n    buttons.forEach((button) => {\n      button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.lang === lang))\n    })\n  }\n\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\n    button.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      const lang = button.dataset.lang\n      if (lang === 'html' || lang === 'vue' || lang === 'markdown') {\n        renderLanguage(lang)\n      }\n    })\n  })\n\n  renderLanguage('html')\n}\n```\n\n## Vue expressions\n\nVue moustache expressions delegate to JavaScript when it is registered:\n\n```vue\n<p>{{ user.name }}</p>\n```\n\n## Svelte expressions\n\nSvelte brace expressions delegate to JavaScript. Svelte control tags remain markup control syntax rather than ordinary JavaScript expressions.\n\n## EJS\n\nEJS regions delegate to JavaScript when available:\n\n```ejs\n<% if (user) { %>\n  <h1><%= user.name %></h1>\n<% } %>\n```\n\n## PHP\n\nRegister `php` to highlight PHP code, including tagless excerpts. Inputs containing `<?php` or `<?=` are treated as documents, with text outside the PHP tags delegated to `html` only when it is registered. Legacy `<?` short tags aren't recognized.\n\n```ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { php } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/php'\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [php, html] })\nconst result = highlighter.highlight('<p><?= $name ?></p>', { lang: 'php' })\n```\n\nPHP does not import HTML. Register `js`, `ts`, and `css` too when the surrounding HTML contains script or style blocks. Quoted strings, including interpolation, and heredoc/nowdoc bodies stay string tokens; Highlight doesn't parse the expressions inside them.\n\n## Markdown fences\n\nThe Markdown definition reads the fence info string and delegates the body:\n\n````md\n```tsx\nconst node = <Button />\n```\n````\n\nBoth `markdown` and `tsx` must be registered. Unknown fence languages receive the `code-inline` class without another tokenizer.\n\n## Recursive template interpolation\n\nJavaScript and TypeScript templates are recursive rather than cross-language embeddings:\n\n```ts\nconst label = `Hello ${user.name.toUpperCase()} ${`#${count}`}`\n```\n\nString chunks remain strings. `${` and `}` are operators, and expression bodies return to the script tokenizer, including nested templates.\n\n## Why dependencies are optional\n\nMaking HTML import JavaScript and CSS would be convenient but would defeat selective modules. Optional delegation keeps import cost explicit and lets a site register one shared JavaScript definition for HTML, Vue, Svelte, EJS, and Markdown.\n\nThis is a focused delegation system, not a general recursive grammar DSL. See [Architecture](../architecture) for the boundary.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Embedded Languages\n---\n\n# Embedded Languages\n\nAn embedded language is a range owned by one language but tokenized by another registered definition.\n\n## Markup\n\nHTML, Vue, and Svelte recognize script and style regions:\n\n```html\n<script>\n  const ready = true\n</script>\n\n<style>\n  .button { color: red }\n</style>\n```\n\nRegister each tokenizer you want used:\n\n```ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, ts, vue],\n})\n```\n\nDefault `<script>` bodies use JavaScript. `<script lang=\"ts\">` uses TypeScript. `<style>` uses CSS.\n\nIf the target definition is absent, the body remains plain text while the outer markup still highlights.\n\n## Compare embedded languages\n\nSwitch the outer language to see registered JavaScript, TypeScript, and CSS tokenizers handle each embedded region.\n\n```ts group=highlight-embedded-languages file=/src/main.ts entry env=client\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { css } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/css'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { js } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/js'\nimport { markdown } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/markdown'\nimport { ts } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/ts'\nimport { tsx } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/tsx'\nimport { vue } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/vue'\nimport { createThemeCss } from '@tanstack/highlight/theme'\nimport { githubDarkTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-dark'\nimport { githubLightTheme } from '@tanstack/highlight/themes/github-light'\n\nconst samples = {\n  html: [\n    '<script>',\n    '  const ready = true',\n    '</script>',\n    '',\n    '<style>',\n    '  .button { color: tomato }',\n    '</style>',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n  vue: [\n    '<script lang=\"ts\">',\n    '  const user: { name: string } = { name: \"Ada\" }',\n    '</script>',\n    '',\n    '<template><p>{{ user.name }}</p></template>',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n  markdown: [\n    '# Typed button',\n    '',\n    '```tsx',\n    'const button = <button>Save</button>',\n    '```',\n  ].join('\\n'),\n}\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [css, html, js, markdown, ts, tsx, vue],\n})\nconst themeCss = createThemeCss({\n  light: githubLightTheme,\n  dark: githubDarkTheme,\n  darkSelector: '.dark',\n})\n\nexport default function render(output: HTMLElement) {\n  const style = document.createElement('style')\n  style.textContent = `${themeCss}\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 24px; font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui; }\n.demo { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); border-radius: 12px; }\n.tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; padding: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent); }\n.tabs button { padding: 6px 10px; border: 0; border-radius: 7px; background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }\n.tabs button[aria-pressed=\"true\"] { background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 12%, transparent); font-weight: 600; }\npre.th-code { margin: 0; min-height: 180px; }\ncode { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }`\n\n  document.head.append(style)\n  output.innerHTML = `<section class=\"demo\">\n  <div class=\"tabs\">\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"html\" aria-pressed=\"true\">HTML</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"vue\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Vue</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-lang=\"markdown\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Markdown</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"output\"></div>\n</section>`\n\n  const codeOutput = output.querySelector('.output')\n  const buttons = output.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang]')\n\n  function renderLanguage(lang: keyof typeof samples) {\n    if (!(codeOutput instanceof HTMLElement)) return\n    codeOutput.innerHTML = highlighter.highlight(samples[lang], { lang }).html\n    buttons.forEach((button) => {\n      button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.lang === lang))\n    })\n  }\n\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\n    button.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      const lang = button.dataset.lang\n      if (lang === 'html' || lang === 'vue' || lang === 'markdown') {\n        renderLanguage(lang)\n      }\n    })\n  })\n\n  renderLanguage('html')\n}\n```\n\n## Vue expressions\n\nVue moustache expressions delegate to JavaScript when it is registered:\n\n```vue\n<p>{{ user.name }}</p>\n```\n\n## Svelte expressions\n\nSvelte brace expressions delegate to JavaScript. Svelte control tags remain markup control syntax rather than ordinary JavaScript expressions.\n\n## EJS\n\nEJS regions delegate to JavaScript when available:\n\n```ejs\n<% if (user) { %>\n  <h1><%= user.name %></h1>\n<% } %>\n```\n\n## PHP\n\nRegister `php` to highlight PHP code, including tagless excerpts. Inputs containing `<?php` or `<?=` are treated as documents, with text outside the PHP tags delegated to `html` only when it is registered. Legacy `<?` short tags aren't recognized.\n\n```ts\nimport { createHighlighter } from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\nimport { html } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/html'\nimport { php } from '@tanstack/highlight/languages/php'\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({ languages: [php, html] })\nconst result = highlighter.highlight('<p><?= $name ?></p>', { lang: 'php' })\n```\n\nPHP does not import HTML. Register `js`, `ts`, and `css` too when the surrounding HTML contains script or style blocks. Quoted strings, including interpolation, and heredoc/nowdoc bodies stay string tokens; Highlight doesn't parse the expressions inside them.\n\n## Markdown fences\n\nThe Markdown definition reads the fence info string and delegates the body:\n\n````md\n```tsx\nconst node = <Button />\n```\n````\n\nBoth `markdown` and `tsx` must be registered. Unknown fence languages receive the `code-inline` class without another tokenizer.\n\n## Recursive template interpolation\n\nJavaScript and TypeScript templates are recursive rather than cross-language embeddings:\n\n```ts\nconst label = `Hello ${user.name.toUpperCase()} ${`#${count}`}`\n```\n\nString chunks remain strings. `${` and `}` are operators, and expression bodies return to the script tokenizer, including nested templates.\n\n## Why dependencies are optional\n\nMaking HTML import JavaScript and CSS would be convenient but would defeat selective modules. Optional delegation keeps import cost explicit and lets a site register one shared JavaScript definition for HTML, Vue, Svelte, EJS, and Markdown.\n\nThis is a focused delegation system, not a general recursive grammar DSL. See [Architecture](../architecture) for the boundary.\n"}
